                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mycetoma",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ef61259-a1e5-3a83-ab6e-7dfb72b2539d",
                                        "entry_id": "3add0a57-7eca-33a6-bcf9-60bb17d32b6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chronic subcutaneous inflammation caused by infection with certain bacteria or fungi."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97de6b5f-c3f1-45bf-8e7d-5b809b928ddd",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef61259-a1e5-3a83-ab6e-7dfb72b2539d",
                                                "text": "black mycetoma"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8722c48e-043c-416d-a56e-0125a4e30ad8",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef61259-a1e5-3a83-ab6e-7dfb72b2539d",
                                                "text": "melanoid mycetoma"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3779bd7-5339-4f45-a82e-1e951a100476",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef61259-a1e5-3a83-ab6e-7dfb72b2539d",
                                                "text": "white mycetoma"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbb56bb8-6eb6-47f4-a939-5f43b9102c62",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef61259-a1e5-3a83-ab6e-7dfb72b2539d",
                                                "text": "ochroid mycetoma"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4b590b0-b04c-4bf1-bdcb-f59482010b12",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef61259-a1e5-3a83-ab6e-7dfb72b2539d",
                                                "text": "The world's only research centre on mycetoma, a neglected tropical disease common among farmers, has been destroyed in Sudan's two-year war, its director and another expert have said. Mycetoma is caused by bacteria or fungus and usually enters the body through cuts. It is a progressively destructive infectious disease of the body tissue, affecting skin, muscle and even bone. It is often characterised by swollen feet, but can also cause barnacle-like growths and club-like hands. \"The centre and all its infrastructure were destroyed during the war in Sudan,\" Ahmed Fahal, director of the Mycetoma Research Centre (MRC), said. \"We lost the entire contents of our biological banks, where there was data from more than 40 years,\" said Fahal, whose centre had treated thousands of patients from Sudan and other countries. \"It's difficult to bear.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98d76562-a383-372c-9a5a-ceb641aeb1d5",
                                        "entry_id": "3add0a57-7eca-33a6-bcf9-60bb17d32b6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chronic subcutaneous inflammation caused by infection with certain bacteria or fungi.",
                                            "Specifically, the Madura foot form of the eumycetoma form of the disease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49316110-0f38-4094-a558-eda1f5e3b60c",
                                                "sense_id": "98d76562-a383-372c-9a5a-ceb641aeb1d5",
                                                "text": "Madura foot, or mycetoma, is a chronic inflammatory disease of the foot terminating in extensive undermining of the tissues by sinuses and cavities. In certain districts blackish masses of fungoid capsules and filaments (chionyphe Carteri) are found in the discharges; and with these, or existing alone in other cases, are yellowish particles, which appear to be simply of fatty composition. It is uncertain whether the parasite is a cause or a complication of the disease. The affection is usually very chronic, and rarely repays attempts at conservative treatment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2566fedc-0c6c-4005-b84d-c4f58f7a8161",
                        "source_entry_id": "12662678-d1e7-30fe-876f-048bfc9f4fe4",
                        "source_sense_id": "eae635cc-fb5c-3412-b3e0-4146b74cda03",
                        "target_lang_word": "mycétome",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mycétome",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b083484-f124-3d1f-91a8-360d7d418d95",
                                        "entry_id": "fc2ee51d-4c91-35dd-aa34-272aee24f495",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pseudo-tumeur inflammatoire sous-cutanée résultant d’une infection par un champignon parasite associé à une bactérie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99aaa98b-a79b-42d7-88d1-6c7cb23fb2e7",
                                                "sense_id": "0b083484-f124-3d1f-91a8-360d7d418d95",
                                                "text": "Les mycétomes sont endémiques dans les régions tropicales sèches du globe, de part et d’autre du 15e parallèle nord (ceinture des mycétomes). Les trois principaux foyers sont l’Inde, l’Afrique sahélienne (en particulier le Soudan) et le Mexique."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3bfd819-2fbe-3a87-a57b-73c5020244e1",
                                        "entry_id": "fc2ee51d-4c91-35dd-aa34-272aee24f495",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Organe spécialisé présent le long du tube digestif chez certains insectes (par ex. anoploures, tipules, etc.) abritant, au sein de cellules particulières appelées mycétocytes, des levures endosymbiotiques en population mixte (c.-à-d. comprenant aussi des bactéries) ou non, et procurant à l’hôte des nutriments indispensables (par ex. vitamines, acides aminés essentiels, etc.) en échange de la protection et du ravitaillement en substrats énergétiques et constitutifs (glucides, lipides, etc.) que leur procure l’insecte hôte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec7a2fdf-53c9-45b1-830e-9357e69076ab",
                                                "sense_id": "a3bfd819-2fbe-3a87-a57b-73c5020244e1",
                                                "text": "Un mycétome est essentiellement un bactériome abritant des levures endosymbiotiques au lieu de, ou en plus de bactéries."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
